  "summary_en": "South Dakota Codified Laws Chapter 50-15 regulates drone operation: requires FAA compliance, criminalizes flights over prisons and military sites, contraband delivery, privacy violations, careless operation and trespass, authorizes counter-drone measures, and limits local and state regulation in deference to federal airspace authority.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Drone operations must comply with FAA regulations; military drones exempt.",
   "Flying over prisons or military facilities is a Class 6 felony; law enforcement may use countermeasures.",
   "Drone delivery of contraband to prisons is a felony.",
   "Privacy invasion, careless/harassing operation and trespass landings are Class 1 misdemeanors.",
   "State and local governments barred from regulating drone design, registration, airspace or pilot qualifications; federal airspace authority preserved."
